// src/v4/workflow/bootstrap.dag
//
// Scope: bootstrap orchestration AS DATA — the seed-once → self-host →
//        fixed-point chain expressed as a .dag workflow, NOT a build.rs
//        or shell script. v2's interpreter (`v2-compiler run`) executes
//        this workflow; every step is data, so the bootstrap orchestration
//        carries zero editable Rust authority.
// Anchor: THESIS:223-226 (meta-process: "Bootstrap, CI, build orchestration
//         ... modeled as .dag workflows") + docs/design-pure-bootstrap-zero.md
//         §"N=0 runtime boundary" (seed is external-to-v4; here in-repo as
//         frozen src/v2/, not in src/v4/)
//
// Owns:
//   - BootstrapPlan: the ordered step sequence
//     - Step seed:   v2-compiler compile --source-root src/v4 → emit Rust
//                    to build-dir → rustc → v4-stage0 binary  (v2 = seed,
//                    touched EXACTLY ONCE; v2's Rust lives in src/v2/,
//                    outside src/v4/, and is frozen/CI-gated)
//     - Step self0:  v4-stage0 compile src/v4 → emit Rust (v4's OWN
//                    emission style) → rustc → v4-stage1
//     - Step self1:  v4-stage1 compile src/v4 → emit Rust → rustc → v4-stage2
//     - Step fixpt:  assert stage1-emitted == stage2-emitted (BitIdentical);
//                    fixed point is stage1==stage2 (NOT stage0==stage1 —
//                    stage0 is v2-emission-style, stage1+ is v4-style)
//   - artifact pinning: v4-stage-final binary is content-addressed; its
//     hash is the anti-regression anchor (T-15 BitIdentical TestClaim)
//
// A3 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15) — the retirement predicate, honestly:
//   - `retired` is NOT a count of hand-Rust files (v3's gameable proxy —
//     defeated by paper-shrink: template-relocation, module-relocation).
//     It is a REPRODUCTION: rebuild from (.dag + frozen-pinned seed) ONLY
//     reproduces the pinned hash AND the seed's own hash matches its pin.
//     `HandResidual` = the Rust the .dag-rebuild cannot reproduce —
//     empty BY REPRODUCTION, never BY COUNT.
//   - This is NOT un-gameable (no structural mechanism is — Trusting-Trust;
//     the pin/CI/seed are all editable by whoever commits). Its job is
//     EARLY, LOUD SURFACING: run per-PR on the affected set (T-21/T-24) so
//     a gaming attempt (un-pin/edit seed, relocate Rust authority, add a
//     7th connective) is un-missable and routes to operator ratification
//     the same commit — not silent drift found months later.
//   - Seed trust is a NAMED AXIOM (built in the open, pinned at a known-
//     good point), not a proof — stated honestly per feedback_no_engine.
//     Any edit to / growth of src/v2/ is the maximally-conspicuous signal
//     = STOP (INVARIANTS:136 bounded seed), routed to the operator.
//   - Actual enforcement = operator-ratification spine + STOP-and-escalate
//     culture + no proxy ratchet to game. Structure makes defection
//     conspicuous, not impossible.
//   - A4 corollary: a 7th connective / 6th behavior is the SAME machine —
//     it changes the reproduction → conspicuous signal → STOP → human
//     judgment. Not "the substrate refuses by construction."
//   - PROOF-1 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15) — the EXTERNAL trust-
//     discharge: gunbc's structural evidence (A2 descent, the algebra-
//     homomorphism chain, cost, effects) is emitted as a machine-
//     checkable proof term an external Lean/Coq KERNEL checks. Converts
//     the seed-trust NAMED AXIOM above into an INTERSUBJECTIVE check
//     against an anchor gunbc does not own — does NOT make it
//     un-gameable (the external kernel + evidence-faithfulness are the
//     new named axioms; trust MOVED, not eliminated). The lens exports
//     witnesses already held; the prover only kernel-checks, never
//     searches (no-engine + A2). Full framing: STRUCTURE.md §7 +
//     DECISIONS.md PROOF-1.
//
// Discipline:
//   - This file is the ONLY bootstrap authority. No build.rs, no bootstrap.sh.
//     A worker reaching for shell/build.rs orchestration has reintroduced
//     editable Rust authority = STOP signal (the v3 regression door).
//   - v2 interprets this (`v2-compiler run workflow/bootstrap.dag`) — v2 is
//     never compiled INTO v4; it is the external frozen seed.
//   - Emitted Rust is transient (build-dir; option (a)); never committed,
//     never editable authority. .dag is sole authority.
//
// Consumes:
//   - extdeps/process.dag: spawn v2-compiler / rustc / v4-stage-N subprocesses
//   - extdeps/file_system.dag: read src/v4/*.dag, write build-dir Rust
//   - std/diagnostic.dag: fail-closed on any step
//   - std/verification.dag: BitIdentical TestClaim for the fixed-point assert
//
// Status: filled (declarative core — T-20 incremental scaffold-early
// slice). The BootstrapPlan DATA + the four-step seed→self0→self1→fixpt
// sequence are present and v2-compile-clean (the structural gate). The
// INTERPRETATION of the plan (spawning v2-compiler/rustc/v4-stage-N via
// extdeps/process.dag, reading/writing build-dir via
// extdeps/file_system.dag) and the executable BitIdentical fixed-point
// TestClaim are DEFERRED — see the TRACKED SCAFFOLD note below.
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (read before validating against the anchor)
//
// DATA, not a runner. This file declares the bootstrap chain AS DATA: a
// fixed `BootstrapPlan` record of named `CompileStep` / `FixedPointStep`
// slots that v2's `run` interpreter walks. There is deliberately NO
// orchestration body here —
// no fn that spawns processes, reads the filesystem, or shells out. That
// is exactly the v3 regression door (build.rs / bootstrap.sh = editable
// Rust/script authority). The plan is inert structured data; the
// interpreter that gives it effect is the deferred operation, with a
// named owner and dissolution trigger (below).
//
// WHY `Stage` IS A CLOSED NULLARY SUM. The chain has exactly four named
// artifacts: the frozen external seed (v2, in src/v2/, touched once) and
// the three self-host products stage0/stage1/stage2. `Stage` enumerates
// them; it carries no payload because a stage IS its identity — the
// emission style (stage0 = v2-style, stage1+ = v4-style) and the source
// root (always src/v4) are FACTS about a stage, derivable, not stored
// fields (no non-load-bearing fields — CODING/MODELING discipline). This
// is why the fixed point is `FixedPoint { Stage1, Stage2 }` and NOT
// stage0==stage1: stage0 is v2-emission-style, so only stage1==stage2 is
// the self-host fixed point.
//
// WHY THE PINNED HASH IS NOT A STORED LITERAL. STRUCTURE.md §"Bootstrap
// chain" + the A3 block (above) make the v4 binary a content-addressed
// release artifact pinned at the fixed-point `Hash` (B1, std/node.dag).
// `Hash` is opaque (K-1, no literal constructor): a pin value is
// PRODUCED by `content_hash : Node -> Hash` at interpret time, never
// hand-written here (a hand-written hash would be exactly the editable
// proxy A3 rejects). So the plan stores no `pinned: Hash` field; the
// `FixedPoint` step DECLARES the BitIdentical equality structurally, and
// the executable assertion over real emitted artifacts is T-15's
// `BitIdentical` TestClaim CONSUMING this plan — not authored here.
//
// TRACKED SCAFFOLD (🟡) — operations deferred with owner + trigger, per
// the operator-ratified declarative-now / operations-deferred discipline
// (std/collection.dag #3169, canonical json.dag #3184). NOT improvised
// bodies, NOT bodiless `fn` (frozen v2 rejects bodiless `fn`, DECISIONS
// PARSE-1):
//   (1) `interpret(BootstrapPlan) -> Outcome<Hash>` — walks the steps,
//       spawning v2-compiler/rustc/v4-stage-N (extdeps/process.dag) and
//       reading src/v4/*.dag + writing transient build-dir Rust
//       (extdeps/file_system.dag). Both extdeps files are T-4.5 SCAFFOLD
//       (zero declarations today) — no process/fs carrier exists to
//       consume. Fail-closed: any step → `Rejected { diagnostic }`
//       (std/diagnostic.dag `Outcome<T>`, DECISIONS item I).
//       OWNER/TRIGGER: dissolves when compiler/05_eval.dag (T-22, the
//       PRIMARY execution path that interprets workflow/*.dag) lands AND
//       extdeps/{process,file_system}.dag (T-4.5) are filled.
//   (2) The executable fixed-point assertion (stage1-emitted ==
//       stage2-emitted, BitIdentical) is a `TestClaim`
//       (std/verification.dag, `kind: RoundTrips`) AUTHORED BY T-15, not
//       here — bootstrap.dag declares the `FixedPoint` step it consumes.
//       OWNER/TRIGGER: T-15 fixed-point validation lane.
//   Bounds on use: no consumer reads an `interpret`/run symbol from this
//   file in this PR; the only gate this file rides today is the
//   structural one (it v2-compiles as well-formed data — the existing CI
//   gate, modeled concretely in workflow/ci.dag's v2-compile job).
//
// SHAPE (INVARIANTS P1/P2 — structural NOW, not a deferred check). The
// bootstrap chain is FIXED by STRUCTURE.md §"Bootstrap chain": exactly
// seed→stage0, stage0→stage1, stage1→stage2, then the stage1==stage2
// fixed point — ZERO degrees of freedom (the source/target edges are
// the chain's structural IDENTITY, NOT user configuration). So each of
// the four positions is its OWN distinct SINGLETON type whose edge
// identity IS the type (documented at the type), and `BootstrapPlan` is
// the fixed record of those four slots — it has EXACTLY ONE inhabitant.
// A reordered / duplicated / missing / extra / MIS-WIRED step is
// UNCONSTRUCTIBLE by type: there are no free `Stage` fields for a slot
// name and a payload to disagree about. This is the openai-pro
// REQUEST_CHANGES (2026-05-16) + operator P2 finding resolved: the edge
// identity is structural now, NOT an interpret-time check.
//
// SUPERSESSION (provenance, not silently dropped — diagnostic.dag #3161
// reconcile precedent). This replaces, in order: (i) the original
// `steps: List<BootstrapStep>` (the node.dag `Diff` #3162
// over-general-list anti-pattern); (ii) the interim free-field
// `CompileStep`/`FixedPointStep` records, which still admitted the
// mis-wiring (`seed` typed-valid with `produces: Stage2`) their own
// comments claimed eliminated — the exact P2 illegal-state. The earlier
// "BOUNDED RESIDUAL / YamlInt-lexeme-class / future-grammar deferral"
// is RETRACTED: single-variant singleton step types ARE valid v4
// (verified — v2 parses `type X = X`), so the structural form is
// reachable NOW; the deferral was unnecessary, not a real bounded
// refinement.
//
// LEDGER PROVENANCE. `BootstrapPlan` is a Conj RECORD and the four step
// types are single-variant SINGLETONS — NO Practice-4 🟢/🟡/🔴
// dissolution ledger applies anywhere in this file: Practice 4 binds
// COPRODUCTS (a ≥2-variant choice to dissolve); a record has no choice
// and a one-inhabitant singleton presents no variant set (modeling-
// discipline.md §4). The earlier `Stage` coproduct (with its full
// five-pattern ledger) and the `BootstrapStep` coproduct are BOTH
// REMOVED — the stage/edge identity is now carried by the four
// singleton step-type NAMES, so neither coproduct is reachable and each
// ledger is removed WITH the type it classified. This MOOTS the earlier
// "Stage/BootstrapStep need ledgers" finding by DISSOLUTION (no
// coproduct remains), the same resolution shape already applied to
// `BootstrapStep`.

module v4.workflow.bootstrap


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The four chain positions — each a distinct SINGLETON whose EDGE
// IDENTITY is the type itself (no free stage fields ⇒ nothing for a
// slot name and a payload to disagree about; the mis-wiring P2
// illegal-state is unconstructible). The stage vocabulary
// (Seed/Stage0/Stage1/Stage2, STRUCTURE.md §"Bootstrap chain") is
// embedded in these names; there is no separate `Stage` enum (removed —
// see LEDGER PROVENANCE). A single-variant `type X = X` is a unit, not
// a coproduct — no Practice-4 ledger applies.

// Seed-once compile: the frozen external v2 seed (src/v2/, touched
// EXACTLY ONCE) compiles src/v4/*.dag → the v4-stage0 binary (v2
// emission style). THE seed boundary.
type SeedToStage0 = SeedToStage0

// Self-host compile: v4-stage0 compiles src/v4/*.dag → v4-stage1
// (v4's OWN emission style — the first self-host product).
type Stage0ToStage1 = Stage0ToStage1

// Self-host compile: v4-stage1 compiles src/v4/*.dag → v4-stage2.
type Stage1ToStage2 = Stage1ToStage2

// Fixed-point assertion: v4-stage1-emitted == v4-stage2-emitted,
// BitIdentical. The self-host fixed point is stage1==stage2 — NOT
// stage0==stage1 (stage0 is v2-emission-style, stage1+ is v4-style).
// The executable assertion is T-15's `RoundTrips` TestClaim consuming
// this step (deferred — TRACKED SCAFFOLD (2) above).
type FixptStage1Stage2 = FixptStage1Stage2


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// BootstrapPlan — the bootstrap chain AS DATA. A FIXED RECORD whose
// four NAMED slots each have a distinct singleton edge-identity type,
// so the seed-once→stage0→stage1→stage2→fixed-point sequence IS the
// type and `BootstrapPlan` has EXACTLY ONE inhabitant — reorder /
// duplicate / missing / extra / mis-wire are ALL unconstructible
// (INVARIANTS P1/P2, structural now). The pinned content-hash is NOT a
// stored field — produced by `content_hash` (B1) at interpret time,
// asserted by T-15.
type BootstrapPlan {
  seed: SeedToStage0
  self0: Stage0ToStage1
  self1: Stage1ToStage2
  fixpt: FixptStage1Stage2
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The canonical (and ONLY constructible) bootstrap plan — STRUCTURE.md
// §"Bootstrap chain" AS DATA. This is the ONLY bootstrap authority;
// v2's `run` interpreter walks THIS. By construction there is exactly
// one inhabitant, so this `data` is not "the correct wiring among
// many" — it is the sole representable value.
data bootstrap_plan: BootstrapPlan = BootstrapPlan {
  seed: SeedToStage0,
  self0: Stage0ToStage1,
  self1: Stage1ToStage2,
  fixpt: FixptStage1Stage2
}

